grund schema — the kinds, places, shapes and citation rules a repository is held to.

Usage:  grund schema [PATH] [--format table|mermaid|dot]

Reads only the effective grund.toml discovered from PATH: no scan, so a broken tree still shows.

Options:
  --format table|mermaid|dot
                       table (default): the terminal view, with a legend.
                       mermaid, dot: the same facts as Mermaid or Graphviz source; grund runs neither.
                       e.g. grund schema --format mermaid
  --path-base project|invocation
                       project (default) spells report paths from the config root;
                       invocation: relative to the path you passed, or the current directory if you passed none.
                       e.g. grund schema docs/ --path-base=invocation

PATH defaults to `.`; config is discovered by walking up from it.
At a workspace root the root project is shown, with one line naming its members.

Exit:  0 printed · 2 the config couldn't be read, or a usage error.

Examples:
  grund schema                         # the quick terminal view
  grund schema --format mermaid        # Mermaid source, e.g. for a GitHub comment
  grund schema --format dot | dot -Tsvg > schema.svg
  grund schema docs/ --path-base=invocation

Guide:    https://github.com/agent-grounds/grund/blob/main/docs/user-facing/schema.md
Example:  https://github.com/agent-grounds/grund/tree/main/examples/schema
